## 12. Why It Works

* `strcpy + strcat` → unsafe
* Buffer only 64 bytes
* Greeting length increases overflow size
* Environment variables store shellcode
* Return address hijacked → jump to shellcode

---

## 13. Key Takeaways

* Environment variables are powerful attack vectors
* Buffer size + string length = critical
* Same code → different behavior based on inputs
* NOP sled improves reliability

